.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt MKBOOTARCHIVE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mkbootarchive
.Nd build an AArch64 boot archive
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Fl o Ar archive
.Oo Ar name Ns = Oc Ns Ar file Ar ...
.Nm
.Fl t Ar archive
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
packs the boot images of a MINIX system into a single file for the AArch64
kernel to unpack at boot.
.Pp
A device tree can name one extra memory range,
.Pa /chosen/linux,initrd-start
and
.Pa -end ,
while the kernel needs a dozen separate ELF images.
The loader is therefore handed one blob holding all of them behind a small
index, and
.Nm
is what writes it.
The kernel reads the index in
.Fn pre_init ,
matches the names against its boot image table, and enters each image in the
module list.
.Pp
Each argument names one image.
A bare
.Ar file
is stored under its last path component; the
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar file
form stores it under
.Ar name
instead, which is what a build needs when the binary sits in a per-program
object directory under a name of its own.
Names are at most 32 bytes.
Every image must be an ELF file.
.Pp
The order of the arguments is the order of the index, but the kernel matches
by name, so it does not have to agree with the kernel's boot image table.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o Ar archive
Write the archive to
.Ar archive .
.It Fl t Ar archive
Print the table of contents of an existing archive and exit.
.It Fl v
Print the table of contents of the archive being written.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/include/aarch64/bootarchive.h
The format, as both this program and the kernel read it.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build an archive of the twelve boot images in the order the kernel's boot
image table lists them, and show what went in:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mkbootarchive -v -o boot.mba ds rs pm sched vfs memory \e
    tty mib vm pfs mfs init
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr boot 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
appeared in MINIX 3 with the AArch64 port.
.Sh BUGS
Numbers in the archive are little-endian, and the kernel does not byte-swap
them.
A big-endian AArch64 target would need both ends changed; the magic number
would not match in the meantime, so it would be noticed rather than
misread.
